Here is a formal patent method claim drafted according to standard patent drafting guidelines (US/EP style).

***

**1.** A computer-implemented method for thematically grouped visual presentation of electronic raw data sets, the method comprising:

1. **receiving**, by one or more processors, an electronic raw data set comprising a plurality of data items, wherein each data item includes at least one of a time specification or an identification (ID) specification;
2. **transforming**, by the one or more processors, the electronic raw data set into a mathematical data structures comprising a plurality of feature vectors and at least one high-dimensional data matrix;
3. **performing**, by the one or more processors, one or more matrix calculations on the at least one high-dimensional data matrix to calculate thematic relationships, wherein the matrix calculations generate at least one of clusters, associations, classifications, or summarizations of the raw data set;
4. **applying**, by the one or more processors, a dimensionality reduction operation to the calculated thematic relationships to map the data items into a two-dimensional (2D) coordinate space;
5. **generating**, by the one or more processors, a three-dimensional (3D) result space by combining the 2D coordinate space with a third axis, wherein the third axis is defined by the time specification or the ID specification of the data items; and
6. **rendering for display**, on a graphical user interface, a final visual 3D presentation of the 3D result space, wherein the data items are visually displayed as thematically grouped representations arranged along the third axis according to their respective time specification or ID specification.
